1210: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
1211: </table>
1212: <p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.</span></p>
1213: </div>
1214: </div>
1215: <div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
1216: <h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
1217: <div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
1218: <p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The RGO potential has Hessian between
1219: <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math>. The
1220: Brascamp–Lieb covariance inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> gives</span></p>
1221: <table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">
1222: 
1223: <tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1224: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1225: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1226: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
1227: </table>
1228: <p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the reverse bound, the
1229: Cramér–Rao inequality (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Theorem 3.5.8]</cite>) gives</span></p>
1230: <table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">
1231: 
1232: <tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1233: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1234: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1235: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
1236: </table>
1237: <p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute both bounds in
1238: (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).
1239: ∎</span></p>
1240: </div>
1241: </div>
1242: <div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
1243: <p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following is the key estimate that decomposes the stochastic gradient error into a bias term and a stochastic error term.</p>
1244: </div>
1245: <div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
1246: <h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stochastic gradient estimates)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
1247: <div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
1248: <p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write</span></p>
1249: <table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">
1250: 
1251: <tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1252: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1253: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)+\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\,,\qquad\mathbb{E}\xi_{\eta}(y;G)=0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)+\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\,,\qquad\mathbb{E}\xi_{\eta}(y;G)=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1254: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
1255: </table>
1256: <p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for all <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,y,y^{\prime},G,G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,y,y^{\prime},G,G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
1257: <table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">
1258: 
1259: <tbody id="S4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1260: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1261: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1262: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1263: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
1264: <td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
1265: <tbody id="S4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1266: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1267: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\langle u,\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\langle u,\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1268: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant e^{\eta\,\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant e^{\eta\,\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1269: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
1270: <td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
1271: <tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1272: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1273: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y^{\prime};G)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y^{\prime};G)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1274: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1275: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
1276: <td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
1277: <tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
1278: <td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
1279: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G^{\prime})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G^{\prime})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
1280: <td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
